# Deny-by-default build context for runtime/arap-cpu/Dockerfile.
#
# The image is built from the REPOSITORY ROOT (`docker build -f
# runtime/arap-cpu/Dockerfile .`) because it ships four reference scripts
# that live under remotion/scripts. A root context would otherwise hand the
# daemon node_modules, .git, dist and every .env in the tree.
#
# So: exclude everything, then re-admit exactly the files the Dockerfile
# COPYs. This is the same posture as the GPU worker image — the COPY list is
# one lock and this file is the second, and neither is the only one. A file
# that is not named twice cannot enter the build at all, which is what makes
# a stray credential structurally impossible rather than merely unlikely.
*

!runtime/arap-cpu/pins.json
!runtime/arap-cpu/entrypoint.sh
!runtime/arap-cpu/proofs
!remotion/scripts/l3_animate_reference.py
!remotion/scripts/autorig_reference.py
!remotion/scripts/segment_reference.py
!remotion/scripts/retarget_armdamped_reference.yaml
